{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"find /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/11 -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort | xargs -r -I{} sh -c 'printf \\\"=== %s ===\\\\n\\\" \\\"\"'$1\"; sed -n \"1,220p\" \"$1\"'\"' sh {}\"","aggregated_output":"=== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/11/des.md ===\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据封闭区域内部\"种子\"像素的颜色，从色板区域查找对应的填充图案，将该图案平铺填满整个封闭区域。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格中有若干由 grey 像素围成的封闭区域（grey 像素构成宽度为 1 的闭合边框，形状为矩形或 L 形等简单多边形）。\n  - 每个封闭区域内部恰好有一个非 black、非 grey 的\"种子\"像素（例如 red、blue、green 等），其余内部像素为 black。\n  - 网格底部（或右侧）有一个用 grey 横线分隔的色板区域，色板区域被分成若干小格，每小格左上角是一个颜色标记像素（与种子颜色一一对应），其余部分是一个 2x2 或 3x3 的小图案（由两种颜色交替构成，如棋盘格、条纹等）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：识别色板区域中每个小格的颜色标记（左上角像素颜色），以及该标记对应的填充图案（小格内除标记外的 2x2 或 3x3 区域）。\n  - 第二步：对网格中每个 grey 封闭区域，读取其内部种子像素的颜色，到色板中查找颜色标记匹配的小格，取出对应的填充图案。\n  - 第三步：将该填充图案以平铺方式（从封闭区域的左上内角开始重复铺设）填满整个封闭区域的内部（覆盖原来的 black 和种子像素），grey 边框保持不变。\n  - 色板区域本身在输出中被清除为 black。\n\n- `Key insight`：种子像素不是输出内容的一部分，而是一个索引键——它指向色板中的某个图案模板；真正的推理难点在于发现色板的编码方式（标记像素 + 图案区域的分离），以及图案是被平铺而非单次放置。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中散落的单色碎片按颜色分组，每组碎片拼合成一个完整矩形，再根据矩形面积从小到大依次嵌套堆叠到输出网格中心。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格中有若干不同颜色的 4-连通碎片对象（例如 red 碎片 2 块、blue 碎片 3 块、green 碎片 2 块）。\n  - 同一颜色的所有碎片可以通过平移（不旋转、不翻转）无重叠地拼合成一个实心矩形。\n  - 不同颜色拼成的矩形面积各不相同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：按颜色将碎片分组，对每组碎片找到唯一的平移拼合方案，确定该颜色对应的完整矩形的尺寸。\n  - 第二步：按拼合后矩形的面积从小到大排序。\n  - 第三步：在输出网格中，以网格中心为对齐点，先绘制面积最大的矩形（最底层），再依次将较小的矩形居中覆盖在上面，形成同心嵌套效果。最小面积的矩形在最顶层。\n  - 输出网格大小等于最大矩形的尺寸加上四周各 1 像素的 black 边距。\n\n- `Key insight`：碎片的空间位置是干扰项——需要先忽略位置，按颜色分组后发现\"碎片拼矩形\"的隐藏关系；然后面积排序决定嵌套层序，这是第二层需要归纳的规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：利用网格边缘的\"指令条\"编码行列操作序列，对内部图案依次执行镜像翻转和颜色替换操作。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格的最外一圈是\"指令框\"：顶边和底边各有一行像素，左边和右边各有一列像素，其余位置为 black。\n  - 顶边的像素序列从左到右编码列操作：red 表示\"该列做上下翻转\"，black 表示\"该列不操作\"。\n  - 左边的像素序列从上到下编码行操作：blue 表示\"该行做左右翻转\"，black 表示\"该行不操作\"。\n  - 右边像素序列从上到下编码颜色替换：每个非 black 像素指定该行内所有 green 像素替换为该像素的颜色。\n  - 底边像素序列从左到右编码颜色替换：每个非 black 像素指定该列内所有 yellow 像素替换为该像素的颜色。\n  - 内部区域（去掉最外一圈后）是一个由 green、yellow 和 black 构成的图案。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：读取顶边指令，对每个标记为 red 的列，将内部区域中该列的像素序列上下翻转。\n  - 第二步：读取左边指令，对每个标记为 blue 的行，将内部区域中该行的像素序列左右翻转。\n  - 第三步：读取右边指令，对指定行执行 green → 对应颜色 的替换。\n  - 第四步：读取底边指令，对指定列执行 yellow → 对应颜色 的替换。\n  - 输出为仅包含内部区域的网格（去掉指令框），尺寸缩小。\n\n- `Key insight`：四条边各自编码不同类型的操作（空间变换 vs 颜色替换），解题者必须分别破译每条边的含义，并发现操作的先后顺序（先翻转再换色）影响最终结果——仅从一个样例无法区分顺序，需要多个样例交叉验证。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据\"路径模板\"对象的走向和\"染色源\"像素的位置关系，沿路径模板的轨迹方向向外扩展色带，色带长度由染色源到路径的距离决定。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格中有若干由 grey 像素构成的连续路径对象（宽度为 1 像素的折线或直线段，4-连通），每条路径长度不超过 15 像素。\n  - 每条 grey 路径的一侧（上方、下方、左方或右方）恰好有一个彩色\"染色源\"像素（非 black、非 grey），距离路径 1 到 5 个像素。\n  - 不同路径的染色源颜色可以不同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：对每条 grey 路径，找到其关联的染色源像素，确定染色源相对于路径的方向（例如染色源在路径的上方）。\n  - 第二步：从路径的每个像素出发，向染色源的**反方向**逐格扩展，扩展长度等于染色源到路径最近像素的格数（按正交方向逐行/列计数）。\n  - 第三步：扩展出的像素全部涂为染色源的颜色。路径本身的 grey 像素保持不变。染色源像素在输出中被清除为 black。\n  - 若扩展过程中遇到其他非 black 像素则停止该方向的扩展。\n\n- `Key insight`：染色源像素同时编码了两个信息：它的颜色决定扩展色带的颜色，它到路径的距离决定色带的长度，而扩展方向是染色源方向的反方向——解题者需要从样例中发现\"距离→长度\"和\"方向取反\"这两条隐藏规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将散落的彩色像素对按连线方向分类，用每对像素的颜色到查找表中获取填充色，在两像素之间的矩形区域内填充该色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格中散布着若干成对出现的彩色像素。每对像素由相同颜色构成，且每种颜色恰好出现两次（例如两个 red、两个 blue、两个 green）。\n  - 网格的某一角落（例如右下角）有一个用 grey 边框围起来的小型\"查找表\"区域，表内是一个 2 列 N 行的网格：左列是颜色样本，右列是对应的填充颜色。查找表中每相邻两行构成一个互换对（第 1-2 行互为一对，第 3-4 行互为一对，以此类推）。\n  - 成对像素的连线方向只有水平和垂直两种情况。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：找到所有同色像素对，确定每对的连线方向（水平或垂直）。\n  - 第二步：对于水平对，在查找表中匹配其颜色所在行，取右列颜色作为填充色。\n  - 第三步：对于垂直对，在查找表中匹配其颜色所在行，取右列颜色后，再查找该颜色在查找表中所在互换对的另一行的右列颜色，以此作为最终填充色。\n  - 第四步：用确定的填充色填满两像素之间的轴对齐矩形区域（包含两端像素所在的行列之间的所有像素），原始的两个端点像素保留其原色不被覆盖。\n  - 查找表区域在输出中保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：第一层推理是发现像素成对并需要查表获取填充色；第二层推理是发现水平对和垂直对使用了不同的查表规则——垂直对需要额外一步互换映射，这从单个样例无法看出，需要对比水平对和垂直对的样例才能归纳出方向依赖的查表差异。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：识别网格中由边框颜色编码的\"容器\"嵌套层级关系，将最内层容器中的图案逐级向外平铺复制，并按层级替换颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格中有若干嵌套的矩形边框（宽度为 1 像素），每层边框颜色不同（例如最外层 red、中间层 blue、最内层 green），层与层之间有 black 间隔。\n  - 最内层边框内部包含一个由 yellow 和 orange 像素构成的小图案（不超过 4x4）。\n  - 其他层的边框内部（除了被更内层占据的区域外）为 black。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：识别嵌套层级——从最内层到最外层排列所有边框。\n  - 第二步：取最内层边框内部的图案作为\"种子图案\"。\n  - 第三步：在每一层边框的内部空白区域（该层边框与下一层边框之间的环形空间），将种子图案平铺填满，但图案的颜色需要替换——将种子图案中的 yellow 替换为该层边框的颜色，orange 保持不变。\n  - 第四步：最内层本身的图案保持原样不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者首先需要发现嵌套层级结构并确定\"从内到外\"的处理顺序，然后发现最内层图案是模板、外层是平铺填充——关键隐蔽性在于颜色替换规则仅替换其中一种颜色（yellow → 边框色），另一种颜色（orange）作为不变锚点，需要从多个样例中比对才能发现。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中的\"信号塔\"像素按臂数量排序，然后按排序顺序在相邻信号塔之间绘制 L 形折线连接。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格中有若干\"信号塔\"结构，每个信号塔由一个中心彩色像素和围绕它的若干同色附属像素组成（中心像素四个正交方向上各最多延伸 1 个同色像素，形成十字形的部分臂，臂数量为 1 到 4 个）。\n  - 不同信号塔的颜色各不相同。\n  - 信号塔之间有足够的空白间距。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：对每个信号塔，数出其臂的数量（中心像素四个正交方向上有几个方向延伸了附属像素），得到该塔的\"级别\"（1 到 4）。\n  - 第二步：按级别从小到大排序；若级别相同，则按从左到右、从上到下的扫描顺序排列。\n  - 第三步：按排序后的顺序，依次在相邻两个信号塔之间绘制 grey 连接线——连接线从第一个塔的中心出发，先水平走到与第二个塔中心同列的位置，再垂直走到第二个塔中心（L 形折线路径），连接线颜色为 grey。\n  - 信号塔自身的彩色像素保持不变，连接线不覆盖已有的信号塔像素。\n\n- `Key insight`：表面上看到的是散落的彩色结构和连接线，但连接顺序既不是空间邻近也不是颜色排列——解题者需要发现\"臂数量\"这个隐藏属性才是排序键，这是第一层推理；第二层推理是发现连接线的\"先水平后垂直\"的固定折线规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据\"钥匙\"形状与\"锁孔\"形状的互补匹配关系，将钥匙对象平移插入对应的锁孔中，并用钥匙的颜色重绘锁的边框。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格中有若干\"锁\"对象：每个锁是一个由单一颜色（如 red、blue 等）绘制的实心矩形，矩形内部挖去了一个不规则的连通孔洞（孔洞像素为 black），孔洞形状各不相同。每个锁的矩形外围还有一圈 1 像素宽的 grey 边框。\n  - 网格中另有若干\"钥匙\"对象：每个钥匙是一个由某种颜色（与锁的填充颜色不同）绘制的不规则小形状，放置在远离锁的位置。\n  - 每把钥匙的形状恰好与某个锁的孔洞形状完全一致（像素级匹配，无需旋转或翻转）。\n  - 钥匙的数量等于锁的数量，且一一匹配。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步：对每把钥匙，遍历所有锁的孔洞，找到形状完全匹配的那个锁。\n  - 第二步：将钥匙平移到对应锁的孔洞位置，用钥匙的颜色填充孔洞（覆盖原来的 black 像素）。\n  - 第三步：将该锁周围的 grey 边框重新涂为钥匙的颜色。\n  - 第四步：清除钥匙原始位置的像素为 black。\n\n- `Key insight`：第一层推理需要发现\"形状互补匹配\"——钥匙的形状等于锁的孔洞形状；第二层推理是发现匹配成功后不仅填充孔洞，还要改变锁的边框颜色——边框颜色变化是容易被忽略的输出差异，需要仔细比对输入输出才能发现。\n</new_puzzle>\n=== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/11/ids.txt ===\ntrain/33067df9\neval/7c66cb00\neval/b0039139\ntrain/8886d717\ntrain/1190bc91\ntrain/758abdf0\neval/16de56c4\neval/65b59efc\ntrain/f3e14006\ntrain/58c02a16\ntrain/e9fc42f2\ntrain/ff2825db\neval/f931b4a8\neval/221dfab4\neval/142ca369\neval/eee78d87\ntrain/57edb29d\ntrain/8fff9e47\ntrain/fd02da9e\ntrain/fe45cba4\n=== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/11/prompt.md ===\n你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"33067df9\" lines=\"32-48\">\n<description>\nExpand the sparse dot lattice into a 26x26 drawing with thick bars between adjacent matching dots.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Foreground pixels lie on logical rows and columns separated by background spacer rows/columns.\n- A logical row or column is present when it contains at least one foreground pixel.\n\nRule\n- Expand every background spacer row/column to thickness 2.\n- Expand the logical rows/columns equally so the full output is 26x26.\n- Paint each foreground logical pixel as a solid rectangle of its color.\n- Connect adjacent same-color logical pixels horizontally through the intervening spacer.\n- Connect adjacent same-color logical pixels vertically only when neither endpoint is part of a horizontal same-color run.\n\nKey insight\n- The input is a sampled line drawing: horizontal same-color runs define the bars first, and only unclaimed same-color vertical neighbors are joined.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"7c66cb00\" lines=\"9-24\">\n<description>\nDock two-tone sprites into color-matched horizontal bars with a color swap.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Top area: small two-tone sprites (outer color + inner color).\n- Below: horizontal bars spanning most of the row, each with a fill color and border color on edges.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the bar whose fill color equals the sprite's outer color.\n- Place the sprite at its original x-position, aligned to the bar's bottom.\n- Recolor: sprite outer → bar border, sprite inner → bar fill.\n- Erase original sprites from the top area.\n\nKey insight: Color matching is inverted — the sprite's dominant color identifies its target bar, then gets swapped to the bar's accent color.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b0039139\" lines=\"29-44\">\n<description>\nRecolor a cropped template and repeat it according to a component-count stencil.\n\nInput structure:\n- Solid blue (1) separator rows or columns split the grid into four sections.\n- Section 1 is a black-background shape template; section 2 is a component-count stencil.\n- Sections 3 and 4 are solid color swatches for output foreground and background.\n\nRule:\n- Crop section 1 to the bbox of its non-black pixels and recolor it with the two swatches.\n- Count 4-connected non-black components in section 2.\n- Repeat the recolored crop that many times, inserting one background-colored row/column between copies.\n\nKey insight: The second section encodes only the repeat count; the output orientation\nis inherited from whether the input separators are columns or rows.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8886d717\" lines=\"43-63\">\n<description>\nRepair markers embedded in the main object and copy the remaining markers one pixel toward the solid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- A mostly background grid contains one solid non-background edge line.\n- Apart from that edge and the background, there is one large main object\n  color and a smaller marker color.\n- Each marker is either embedded in the main object, touching it on at\n  least three 4-neighbor sides, or isolated on the background.\n\nRule:\n- Embedded markers are recolored to the main object color.\n- Isolated background markers remain in place and also paint the adjacent\n  background pixel in the direction of the solid edge line.\n- All other pixels are unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\nThe full edge line is a direction cue: it tells which way the background\nmarkers extend, while markers surrounded by the main object are simply\ndefects to be filled.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"1190bc91\" lines=\"36-49\">\n<description>\nComplete a sparse grid by casting occluding diagonal rays from the longest run and filling the remaining diagonal-connected regions from the short bars.\n\nInput structure\n- Black-background grid with one unique longest 4-connected foreground object.\n- The longest object is a horizontal or vertical multicolor run; all other foreground objects are shorter monochrome bars.\n\nRule\n- On a blank canvas, process the longest run from left to right or top to bottom; each pixel emits four 45-degree rays that stop at the first already-painted pixel.\n- Each remaining monochrome bar fills every still-blank pixel reachable from it by diagonal steps.\n\nKey insight\n- Earlier pixels in the long run occlude later diagonal rays, and those ray barriers partition the background into diagonal-connected regions for the short bars.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"758abdf0\" lines=\"54-69\">\n<description>\nAdvance short marker bars away from the full edge bar, turning completed two-pixel markers into edge-color marks at the opposite side.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One non-background color forms a complete one-cell-thick bar on exactly one outer edge.\n- The other foreground color appears only in the first two cells inward from that bar, lane by lane.\n\nRule\n- In each lane perpendicular to the edge bar, a one-pixel marker adjacent to the bar grows one more cell inward.\n- A two-pixel marker in those first two inward cells is cleared back to background.\n- The cleared two-pixel marker is replaced by a two-pixel mark of the edge-bar color at the opposite side of the same lane.\n\nKey insight\n- The full edge bar defines both the orientation and the direction of the local two-step marker cycle.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"16de56c4\" lines=\"9-34\">\n<description>\nFill periodic progressions that shoot from a unique grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.  Sparse non-bg dots of several colors.\n- All repeating colors originate from the same grid edge (top, bottom,\n  left, or right — the one with the most non-bg dots).\n- Each repeating color has exactly 2 dots per shooting-direction line;\n  their gap defines the step.\n- Every non-bg dot lies on a shooting-direction line that contains a\n  repeating color.\n\nRule:\n- Determine the unique shooting edge; left/right → rows, top/bottom → columns.\n- For each shooting-direction line, the repeating color has exactly 2 dots;\n  step = gap between them, offset = first position mod step.\n- A different-colored dot aligned to the same beat (pos % step == offset) is\n  a companion: it absorbs the ray and becomes the fill color, limiting the\n  fill range to the span between repeating and companion dots.\n- An unaligned dot is a bystander and left untouched.\n- Without a companion the repeating color fills the entire line.\n\nKey insight: the shooting edge is identified by counting boundary dots;\nthe gap between the two marker dots is the period; a companion sharing the\nmodular class acts as a wall that stops the ray and dictates the paint color.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"65b59efc\" lines=\"9-24\">\n<description>\nDecode a stamp map: read templates, markers, and palette from a tiled grid, then render stamps.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid divided into K tile columns (each N wide) separated by 1-col dashed separators.\n- Top band (rows 0..N-1): K template masks, one per tile column.\n- Middle band (rows N+1..2N): marker pixels whose color picks a template.\n- Bottom band (rows 2N+2..): K palette swatches giving the output color per template.\n- Separator rows at rows N and 2N+1 (dashed pattern of sep color).\n\nRule:\n- Each marker's local position (lr, lc) within its tile column determines which N×N output block to stamp.\n- The marker's color identifies which template to use; the palette recolors the template.\n\nKey insight: Marker color encodes template index; local position within tile column encodes stamp block.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f3e14006\" lines=\"21-39\">\n<description>\nBuild the woven rectangle determined by the two marked cells on each crossed bar.\n\nInput structure\nA black-background grid contains one long horizontal bar and one long vertical bar.\nEach bar has a dominant base color and exactly two same-colored marker pixels.\n\nRule\nThe horizontal marker pair gives the output column span.  From the horizontal bar\nrow, walk toward the farther vertical marker; rows and columns alternate every\nother cell.  Even step/even offset cells use the horizontal marker color until\nthe nearer vertical marker is reached, then use the vertical marker color.\nOdd row steps use the horizontal base on marker columns and the original\ncrossing color on spacer columns.  Spacer columns on even row steps use the\nvertical base, except at the switch row where they use the crossing color.\n\nKey insight\nThe original cross cell records which base color wins at base/base lattice\ncrossings; the nearer vertical marker is the color-switch boundary.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"58c02a16\" lines=\"10-26\">\n<description>\nExpand the top-left seed mask into a recursive colored pattern and tile it across the full grid.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- All foreground lies in a top-left rectangle whose last row and last column are a solid secondary color.\n- Removing that secondary-color row and column leaves a seed region containing background plus one primary color.\n\nRule\n- Use the primary-color pixels in the seed as a binary mask.\n- Replace each primary seed cell with a copy of the seed mask in the primary color, and each background seed cell\n  with a copy of the seed mask in the secondary color.\n- Repeat and crop that expanded tile to the original grid shape.\n\nKey insight\nThe solid L-shaped secondary-color border is a legend, not output content; it supplies the color used when the\nseed's background cells are expanded.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
